{"`timezone.now()` is evaluated once at module import time, so every instance that relies on the default will get the same stale timestamp. Use `field(default_factory=timezone.now)` to evaluate it per-instance.": 0.9540692567825317, "Typo in test name: `test_from_dict_inalid_data` should be `test_from_dict_invalid_data` (missing 'v' in 'invalid').": 0.25800326466560364, "Misleading test name: `test_from_dict_empty_array` tests an empty dict, not an array. Consider renaming to `test_from_dict_empty_dict`.": 0.19999511539936066, "`to_dict()` returns the `queued` field as a raw `datetime` object. If this dict is passed as Celery task kwargs (JSON-serialized), this will raise a `TypeError`. Consider converting `queued` to an ISO format string.": 0.889664351940155, "The `assignment_source` parameter added to `sync_status_outbound` is never passed by the `sync_status_outbound` task (the only caller), making it dead code. The status outbound task passes neither `sync_source` to `should_sync(\"outbound_status\")` nor `assignment_source` to `sync_status_outbound()`. Either update the task to propagate this source or remove the parameter.": 0.6745429039001465, "When `AssignmentSource.from_dict` returns `None` due to a parse error, the cycle-prevention logic is silently disabled and the outbound sync proceeds as if no assignment source context exists. Consider logging a warning when `assignment_source_dict` is non-null but `parsed_assignment_source` is `None`.": 0.6653676629066467}